[style name="Interaction_Style"]
if {Ian.Confrontationn_at_home} == 1:
	join Thorinn (normal) leftmost
	Narrator: *Knock knock*
	Ian: Come in.
	[signal arg="start_night"]
	[wait time="2.0" hide_text="false"]
	[background arg="res://gui/Dialog/styles/Finished_Ian_room.webp" fade="0.0"]
	join Ian rightmost
	Thorinn: Good morning. My name is [b]Thorinn[/b], I am a traveling doctor. Hugo sent me, he said you’ve fallen [i]ill[/i].
	Ian: Thorinn... I’ve heard that name before. Where did you study medicine?
	Thorinn: I trained in Stoneleaf under Master Galbraith.
	Ian (angry): [i]Of course[/i]. Galbraith never stopped talking about his ‘most promising student’.
	Thorinn (surprised): So he talked about me? I guess you are lucky to have me then... haha.
	[sound path="res://assets/Sounds/awkward_crickets.mp3" volume="-6.0"]
	Narrator: *A moment of awkward silence*
	Thorinn (normal): That's the [b]reason[/b] I'm here. Our master has taught me well, and I’ve saved many lives. Including yours, if you’ll let me.
	Ian (angry): And why would you [i]want[/i] to save me? What is your motive?
	Ian (angry): You could take my place as the trusted healer the moment I’m gone or even help death along a little faster.
Thorinn (normal): You overestimate my cruelty. I don’t need to hasten your death, Ian.
Thorinn: The villagers will come to me in time, because they’ll [i]see[/i] I’m more capable.
Thorinn: But I came here because it’s what a doctor does. I heal. I leave the rest to fate.
Ian (normal): [b]Fate?[/b] You talk as though you don’t have a hand in it. 
Ian: You’ve been searching for an opportunity like this, haven’t you? To step in and become the [i]savior[/i] of a village.
- Try to save Ian
	set {Ian.Selected_Ian_Choice} = 1
	Thorinn (agitated): I don’t need to take what’s already slipping from your grasp, Ian. 
	Thorinn: This village doesn’t need someone clinging to old ways. They need someone who can do more...
	Thorinn: ...someone who can truly save them. They need me. And I will do whatever is necessary to protect them.
	Ian (sceming): Save them? I’ve cared for these people for years, Thorinn. I know their needs better than you ever will.
	Thorinn (agitated): You’ve cared for them, yes. But have you healed them? 
	Thorinn: Look around, Ian. Already from my way here I could tell that the village is not doing so well, just like you.
	Thorinn: I can even see on your equipment, you hold onto traditions that no longer work. Soon, the village will see it too. 
	Thorinn: They’ll come to me, because they’ll have no other [b]choice.
	Ian (angry): So why save me, then?! If you’re so [i]sure[/i] they’ll turn to you, why bother? To ease your conscience? 
	Ian: Or so I can live long enough to watch you take everything [b]from me?
	Thorinn (normal): I am treating you because that's [i]my job, I heal people.
	Ian (angry): You arrogant fool! Do you think this will make them trust you? I’ll tell them what kind of man you are. 
	Ian: I’ll make sure they see the [b]truth!
	Thorinn (agitated): We’ll see. Now lie still. You don’t have much time, and I won’t let my first victory here be a failure.
	leave --All--
	join Thorinn (surprised) leftmost
	Narrator: *Thorinn retrieves his medical supplies from the inn, but by the time he gets back to the pharmacy Ian has already passed.*
- End Ian’s suffering
	set {Ian.Selected_Ian_Choice} = 2
	Narrator: *Thorinn calmly, pulls a small vial from his bag.*
	Thorinn (normal): But by then, it’ll be too late for you to see it. 
	Thorinn: I’ve prepared [i]something[/i]...a final act of mercy from one healer to another. It will ease your pain.
	Ian (angry): What... what is [i]that?
	Thorinn (normal): A blend of rare herbs, taught to me by our master. It will calm your body and make your life come to a peaceful end.
	Ian (angry): That’s [b]pathetic[/b], you think I will just give up now?
	Thorinn (normal): We [i]both[/i] know that your condition in this state is irreversible, there is nothing anyone could do. 
	Thorinn: The only thing you have a choice in now, is how you die. If you take the potion, it wouldn't be a sign of giving up.
	Thorinn: It would grant you a chance to take matters into [i]your own hands.
	Thorinn: You can either be dreadfully waiting for a painful death, or accept your fate and give yourself a soothing end.
	Ian (normal): You know Thorinn, you might be [i]right.[/i] I think it ends here, but please don’t tell anyone of my cowardice.
	Thorinn (surprised): If that’s the cost, so be it. For now, let this be the end of your [b]suffering.
	Narrator: *Ian, too weak to resist, takes the vial and drinks it. His breaths becoming shallow and laboured.*
	Ian (angry): Treat my people well Thorinn, the village is in your hands now....
	Thorinn (agitated): Don’t worry, I'll take care of them. Rest, Ian. You’ll find peace soon.
	Narrator: *Ian’s body goes limp, his breath slowing until it stops. Thorinn watches for a moment, his face unreadable, then turns away.
	Thorinn: He leaves the pharmacy without a word, stepping into the quiet streets of the village.*
- Refuse to help
	set {Ian.Selected_Ian_Choice} = 3
	Thorinn (agitated): Ian, I [b]didn’t[/b] come to take anything from you. I just came to help. I came here out of respect.
	Ian (angry): [b]Respect?[/b] Is that what you call this? Do you really wish to say that our master has taught you more and better than me?
	Thorinn (normal): [i]I was his best student after all.[/i] But that doesn’t make me your [b]enemy.[/b] Now tell me, do you wish for me to help you or not?
	Ian (angry): Does it [i]really[/i] seem like I need your help? I can take care of myself!
	Thorinn (agitated): Then I won’t, if that’s what you wish, but know that I’ll take over your pharmacy sooner or later.
	Thorinn (normal): And they will turn to me, whether you survive or not.
	Ian (sceming): That remains to be seen, now leave me be. I don’t feel like hearing any more of your [b]arrogant remarks.
	Narrator: *Ian stares at Thorinn, his breathing slowing as his strength fades. Thorinn stands there for a moment, watching, his expression heavy with unspoken emotions. He finally turns to leave.*
	leave Ian
	Thorinn (agitated): Very well, Ian. I’ll leave. [i]The village will remember you...
	Narrator: *Thorinn leaves Ian to his fate. Ian dies shortly after.*
set {Ian.Confrontationn_at_home} = 2
[signal arg="End_Find_Ian"]
[signal arg="end-night"]
[wait time="2.0"]
elif {Astrid.ask_for_help} == 2:
elif {Ian.Confrontationn_at_home} == 2:
	Thorinn: No point going back in there.
